The `for_run_list` iterates `(x) = (x)->next`. When a PDI is processed, it's moved to `explicits_list` via `move_node_before`. Let me look at the PDI handling again to see if the node is moved.

Looking at the code, in the PDI branch, there's no `move_node_before` for the PDI itself. Let me re-read the PDI branch:

```c
else if (this_type == FRIBIDI_TYPE_PDI)
{
  for (i = RL_LEN (pp); i; i--)
  {
    ...
  }
}
```

There's no `move_node_before` in the PDI branch. So the PDI stays in the run list. But the `for_run_list` advances via `(x) = (x)->next`. So after processing a PDI, it moves to the next run.

